==German==

===Etymology===
{{root|de|ine-pro|*deyḱ-}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|zēhe}}, from {{inh|de|goh|zēha}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*taihā}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*taihwǭ||toe}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*deyḱ-||to point out}}. Compare {{cog|nl|teen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈt͡seːə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Zehe.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f}}

# [[clove]] {{gloss|of garlic and similar plants}}
# {{lb|de|regional}} {{alternative form of|de|Zeh|t=toe}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Zehe'' as meaning "toe" is universally understood, but fairly rare in most regions. The form is common in [[Saxony]] (and bordering parts of East Central Germany) as well as parts of [[Austria]].<ref>http://www.atlas-alltagssprache.de/genus/</ref>

